  "parse": {
    "title": "1.x/List of Requirement node types",
    "pageid": 35,
    "revid": 692,
    "text": {
      "*": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en-GB\" dir=\"ltr\"><table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"cellpadding: 5px; text-align: center;width: 100%\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th colspan=\"1\" style=\"width: 100%; background-color:#F75D59; font-size: 32px; padding: 15px;\"><b>Not Supported!</b>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: 16px;\">This page is about Citizens 1.x, while the current version is Citizens 2.0.2. This page's content may be outdated, and shouldn't be trusted as being correct. See this page's talk page for more information. If you were looking for the 2.0.2 equivalent of this page, try <a href=\"/index.php?title=List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"List of Requirement node types (page does not exist)\">List of Requirement node types</a>. If you feel this message was displayed in error, please contact an administrator.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en-GB\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Requirements_node\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Requirements node</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Requirement_Types\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Requirement Types</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#NPC\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">NPC</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Rank\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Rank</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Permission\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Permission</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Quest\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Quest</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Item\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Item</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Health\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Health</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Money\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Money</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading1\"><h1 id=\"Requirements_node\">Requirements node</h1><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Requirements node\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>The requirements node is used in <a href=\"/index.php?title=Quests.yml&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Quests.yml (page does not exist)\">Quests.yml</a> to tell the quester what is required for the the player before the quest can start.  If all the requirements listed in the requirements: node are met, the quest is granted. Requirements share a lot in common with rewards, as most reward types can also be used for requirements. \n</p><p>For example:\n</p>\n<pre>requirements:\n    '0':\n        type: item    # Requires an item.\n        id: 371       # gold_nugget\n        amount: 30\n        take: true    # Takes the gold nuggets from the player.\n    '1':\n        type: quest   # Requires a quest to be completed prior.\n        quest: \"Example Quest\"\n</pre>\n<p>You may have multiple requirements, or just one.  \n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading1\"><h1 id=\"Requirement_Types\">Requirement Types</h1><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Requirement Types\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"NPC\">NPC</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: NPC\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p><i><a href=\"/index.php?title=Notes_from_aufdemrand&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Notes from aufdemrand (page does not exist)\">Notes from aufdemrand</a>: Pretty sure this works, but needs tested to be sure.</i>\n</p><p>NPC requirement (npc:) - requires an NPC to be owned by the player.\nUses a name: node to specify the name of the npc, and a comma-separated list of toggles in the types: node (eg. trader,quester,guard). Will create an NPC owned by the player who completed the quest, with a generated UID.\n</p><p>take: node is optional. Default is take: false.\n</p>\n<pre>'0':\n    type: npc\n    npcid: 1   # id of npc in which to check ownership\n</pre>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Rank\">Rank</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Rank\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Rank requirement (rank) - checks that a player has access to a group ('rank') provided it uses a compatible permissions system.\nSpecified by the rank: node.\n</p><p>take: node is optional. Default is take: false.\n</p>\n<pre>'0':\n    type: rank     # Checks for rank\n    rank: 'admin'  # Quest requires admin rank\n</pre>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Permission\">Permission</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Permission\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Permission requirement (permission) - checks if the player has specified permission.\nSpecified by the permission: node.\n</p><p>take: node is optional. Default is take: false.\n</p>\n<pre>'0':\n    type: permission   # Checks for permission\n    permission: 'modifyworld.blocks.place.4' # Can user place cobblestone?\n</pre>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Quest\">Quest</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Quest\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Quest requirement (quest) - checks to see if a quest has been completed. \nSpecified by the quest: node.\n</p><p>take: node is not supported on the Quest requirement node.\n</p>\n<pre>'0':\n    type: quest\n    quest: 'Slime Slaying I'</pre>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Item\">Item</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Item\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Item reward (item) - checks player for specified items before starting. Items can also be taken upon quest acceptance with take=true.\nLoaded from the item: nodes.\n</p><p>take: node is optional. Default is take: false.\ndata: node is optional.\n</p>\n<pre>'0':\n    type: item    # \n    item:\n    id: 50\n    amount: 50</pre>\n<pre>   take: false   # Only checks for items, does not take them.\n</pre>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Health\">Health</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Health\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p><i><a href=\"/index.php?title=Notes_from_aufdemrand&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Notes from aufdemrand (page does not exist)\">Notes from aufdemrand</a>: Pretty sure this works, but needs tested to be sure.</i>\n</p><p>Health reward (health) - gives health to a player.\nLoaded from the amount: node.\n</p><p>take: node is optional. Default is take: false.\n</p>\n<pre>'0':\n    type: health\n    amount: 10\n</pre>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Money\">Money</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/index.php?title=1.x/List_of_Requirement_node_types&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Money\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Money reward (money) - checks if player has a specified amount of money. Can also be used to take money on quest acceptance.\nLoaded from the money: node.\n</p><p>take: node is optional. Default is take: false.\n</p>\n<pre>'0':\n    type: money\n    money: 100\n    take: true  # Takes money from player </pre>\n<div class=\"padded\" style=\"font-size: 12px; padding: 5px\">\n<table class=\"wikitable collapsible collapsed\" style=\"cellpadding: 5px; text-align: center;width: 100%\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 100%; background-color:#C0C0C0\">Quick Navigation\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width: 15%\"><a href=\"/Category:Usage\" title=\"Category:Usage\">Usage</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"width: 85%\" align=\"left\"><a href=\"/Installation\" title=\"Installation\">Installation</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/Frequently_Asked_Questions\" title=\"Frequently Asked Questions\">Frequently Asked Questions</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/Commands\" title=\"Commands\">Commands</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/Editors\" title=\"Editors\">Editors</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/Characters\" title=\"Characters\">Characters</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/API\" title=\"API\">API</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32;\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width: 15%\"><a href=\"/Category:Configuration\" title=\"Category:Configuration\">Configuration</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"width: 85%\" align=\"left\"><a href=\"/Configuration\" title=\"Configuration\">Configuration</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/Text_Syntax\" title=\"Text Syntax\">Text Syntax</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/Permissions\" title=\"Permissions\">Permissions</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/Waypoints\" title=\"Waypoints\">Waypoints</a> &#160;<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">&#183;</span>&#32; <a href=\"/Data_Storage\" title=\"Data Storage\">Data Storage</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261019145808\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.113 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 90/1000000\nRevision size: 3166/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 2467/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 892/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\n